  "description": "The Backroad Force AXS is an adventure gravel bike with carbon frame that puts the focus on comfort, versatility and cargo capacity. Thanks to features such as the generous tyre clearance of 53 mm, a frame compartment, a detachable frame bag and a USB-C port under the handlebar, it is the perfect companion for long tours in versatile terrain or bikepacking. Characteristics and advantages: The Backroad Force AXS weighs just about 9.1 kg1 and features the electronic SRAM Force AXS 1x13 groupset with a 40-tooth chainring up front and a 10-46-tooth cassette at the rear. The wireless and weight-optimised shifting system allows for a quick, intuitive change of gears at the touch of a button and combines a wide gear range with 13 closely spaced gears. This ensures efficiency in training and reserves on off-road tours. + Lightest and sportiest model + 13 closely spaced gears + Widest range of uses Ideal for: • anyone who appreciates low weight and a performance-oriented gearing with 13 gears • sporty gravel tours and multi-day bikepacking • long climbs and changing terrain • tours on tarmac and rough gravel • riders looking for comfort and control on long distances Less suitable for: • gravel racing with a focus on maximum aerodynamics • technical MTB trails or aggressive off-road riding • short rides focused purely on city riding or everyday use Highlights: • Magnetic Fidlock bag system – including a precisely fitting frame bag (approx. 3 litres) • Integrated frame compartment – space for tools and equipment, including a tool bag • USB-C charging port – power supply directly on the handlebar (power bank required) • 18 attachment points – flexible mounting of bottles, bags and other accessories • Tyre clearance up to 53 mm – more damping and grip on rough terrain • Carbon seat post with a low clamp – comfort through flex Other features: The Backroad Force AXS comes with SRAM's electronic 13-speed gravel groupset of the same name, wide 45 mm Terra Adventure tyres from Continental and robust Rose G30 aluminium wheels (27 mm rim width). A chainguide protects against chain drops and the fi´zi:k Terra Argo X7 saddle ensures sportiness and comfort. The Rose handlebar and stem also allow for attachment of additional parts such as an aerobar or a computer mount. Note: Pedals are not included. ¹ may vary up to +/- 5 % due to manufacturing tolerances, reference frame colour terra, size M/L, without pedals and bags",
